Here is the commit message:
ipvs: skip ipv6 extension headers for csum checks

Protocol checksum validation fails for IPv6 if there are extension
headers before the protocol header. iph->len already contains its
offset, so use it to fix the problem.

Fixes: 2906f66a5682 ("ipvs: SCTP Trasport Loadbalancing Support")
Fixes: 0bbdd42b7efa ("IPVS: Extend protocol DNAT/SNAT and state handlers")
Signed-off-by: Julian Anastasov <ja@ssi.bg>
Signed-off-by: Florian Westphal <fw@strlen.de>

Here is the root cause:
The checksum validation functions for IPv6 (sctp_csum_check, tcp_csum_check, udp_csum_check) incorrectly computed the transport header offset by using sizeof(struct ipv6hdr) instead of the actual offset from the caller, which accounts for IPv6 extension headers. Additionally, for TCP and UDP, the checksum verification used ipv6_hdr(skb)->nexthdr (which may be an extension header number) instead of the actual protocol constant (IPPROTO_TCP or IPPROTO_UDP), leading to false failures when extension headers are present.

